# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/.eggs/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/

# Environment and secrets
.env
*.env
!.env.example
/secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# Account, organization, and instance identifiers. Not credentials, but the repo
# is public and these aid targeting and enumeration. Committed docs use
# placeholders and resolve them from these files.
*.local.md
infra/aws/bootstrap-outputs.env

# Superseded AWS Academy Learner Lab requirements note. Carries a Vocareum
# `vockey` session token inside its URLs, so it must never reach this public
# repository. The Learner Lab path was abandoned 2026-07-30 in favour of a
# dedicated Organizations member account.
claudedocs/mlops_final_project_requrements_aws.md

# Data (raw Jigsaw dataset and derived splits are not versioned in git).
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: an unanchored `data/` matches any directory named
# data at ANY depth, and silently excluded model/data/ -- the whole Phase 0 pipeline --
# from ten commits. Tests passed locally because the files were on disk; a fresh clone
# had no data pipeline at all.
/data/
# ...and the convenience symlink some worktrees carry. It points at an ABSOLUTE path on
# one machine, so committing it gives every fresh clone and every CI runner a dangling
# link, and leaks the developer's directory layout.
/data
*.csv
# ...but the synthetic test fixture is a committed source artifact, not data.
!tests/fixtures/*.csv
*.csv.gz
*.parquet

# Model artifacts (fetched from W&B by digest at deploy time, never committed)
/artifacts/
*.onnx
# ...but the challenger contract's 32-byte digest fixture is a committed source artifact,
# not a model. Same shape as the `!tests/fixtures/*.csv` exception above, and the same
# failure it prevents: a blanket suffix rule that passes locally and produces a
# FileNotFoundError on the first fresh clone. test_committed_test_fixtures_are_tracked
# asserts the property rather than trusting this line.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.onnx
*.skops
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.joblib
*.pkl

# Weights & Biases local run cache
/wandb/

# Test and lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Python virtualenvs
/.venv/
/.venv-lock/
/.venv-scan/

# The checksum-verified gitleaks binary, fetched by scripts/install_gitleaks.sh on the
# runner and on the build box. The checksum is committed (scripts/gitleaks.sha256); the
# 11 MB binary is not.
/bin/

# Raw dataset, fetched by scripts/fetch_jigsaw.sh, never committed
/data/raw/

# Terraform. The lock file IS committed (it pins provider hashes); state and local
# working dirs are not. tfvars may carry the operator CIDR and alert email, so those
# stay out.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
# ...but the pinned AMI IS source. `variables.tf` says ami_id is "supplied by the
# committed infra/terraform/ami.auto.tfvars", and the whole point of pinning it rather
# than resolving the latest AL2023 at plan time is that the value is reviewed. It is
# already tracked, so it survives a fresh clone -- but only because ignore rules do not
# apply to tracked files. Without this exception a rotated AMI silently fails to stage,
# which is the same shape as the unanchored `data/` that hid ten modules for ten commits.
!infra/terraform/ami.auto.tfvars
# ...and the grading-window override, for the same reason: it is a reviewed decision about
# how the stack runs, not an operator's local secret. It disarms the nightly stop so the
# graded stack is up whenever the instructor looks at it. Uncommitted, it would be invisible
# to review and absent from the runner, and the next apply would silently re-arm the
# shutdown -- which is exactly the drift it was written to close.
!infra/terraform/grading.auto.tfvars
# ...and the public demo window, for the third time and the same reason. It opens the three
# graded listeners to the internet so a grader can reach them. It carries no secret -- the
# value is literally 0.0.0.0/0 -- while the operator's own address stays in the gitignored
# tfvars where it belongs. Uncommitted, the next apply would silently re-close the listeners
# and the README's live URLs would start timing out with no error anywhere.
!infra/terraform/demo.auto.tfvars

# RunPod launch registry: runtime state, not source. It records live pod ids so a crash
# between "pod created" and "pod ready" still leaves something terminatable. Committing it
# would ship one machine's live pods to every other clone.
infra/runpod/runpod_pods.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output: browser snapshots and console logs from screenshot runs.
# The screenshots that matter are moved into docs/evidence/screenshots/ deliberately.
.playwright-mcp/
